  body=[{'t':'ul','items':['GE Vernova ended September 2026 with gas equipment backlog and slot reservations at 122 GW, up from 116 GW, and expects at least 130 GW by year-end [@W:gev3q] [@W:gevtm].','Inside that number, firm backlog rose from 53 to 64 GW while reservations fell from 63 to 58 GW as 13 GW converted to orders [@W:gev3q].','New gas contracts slowed to 11 GW in the quarter, from 20 GW in the second [@W:gevmb]. One analysis notes it was the first of five quarterly releases in which reservations fell [@W:gevfw].','Output is planned at 20 GW a year from Q3 2026, 24 GW in 2028 and 30 GW by 2030 [@W:gevq2].','Earlier reporting put delivery of a new combined-cycle plant at about five years, against three and a half in 2023 [@D23].']}],
